 {"id":"AUG-123","status":"blocked","priority":"P1","complexity":4,"title":"[P1] Add first-class XML test and verification obligations, including migration-file coverage","reasoning":"Owner clarification 2026-10-30: specifications must say what tests are required, not merely name a verification method. A database migration requirement must pull in a test that applies the named migration file from the supported prior schema. Scope for THIS row: typed verification/test nodes linked to requirements; stable IDs, active/inactive lifecycle/version, target file or code surface, tracked test path/name, runner/selector metadata, fixture/precondition, expected assertions, and evidence form; query assembly returns only the selected requirements’ test obligations. XML references tracked tests; it never supplies arbitrary shell text for execution. Out of scope: changing production migration files, adding a new test runner, implementing GitReins handoff, or treating a package-suite pass as proof of a migration-specific test. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R15 and #AC-17; depends on AUG-118 for the XML graph.\nch:trace row=AUG-123 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R15 wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/xml-spec-task-tests-gitreins-2026-10-30","acceptance_criteria":"- **AC-17 (T):** Given a requirement linked to a database migration verification node, when Auger assembles the requirement, then the same bundle includes the exact migration path, supported prior-schema fixture, tracked test path/name, runner/selector metadata, expected schema/data assertions, and rollback test obligation when rollback is declared supported; proof: a fixture whose test actually applies the named migration file and fails when that file is replaced by a no-op.\nGiven duplicate, dangling, stale-version, o