 {"id": "AUG-124", "status": "complete", "priority": "P1", "complexity": 5, "title": "[P1] Package canonical boardctl tasks with scoped Auger specs and tests for GitReins judging", "reasoning": "Owner clarification 2026-10-30: GitReins must receive the canonical task from boardctl together with exact spec scope and required test links, then judge from those sources rather than accepting this agent’s summary as truth. Scope for THIS row: read the exact canonical row through the supported boardctl read surface; resolve its spec/test refs through Auger; package board acceptance criteria verbatim, included/excluded block IDs with reasons, active/inactive state, source versions/digests, test refs/runner selectors, and a collision-safe board-ID mapping; validate ch:trace before any GitReins task/judge starts; read back the created GitReins task. Out of scope: direct JSONL writes, a second XML parser/evaluator, changing GitReins internals (GR-155), task dispatch/completion, or treating worker_summary/commit prose as evidence. Source: docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R14, #R16, and #AC-16, #AC-18–AC-20. Depends on AUG-119, AUG-120, AUG-121, AUG-122, and AUG-123; GR-154 is the separately owned GitReins pre-commit task.\nch:trace row=AUG-124 spec=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md#R16 wave=none:task-not-dispatched test=none:not-implemented doc=docs/prd/xml-spec-graph.md prompt=none:not-dispatched evidence=none:not-run witness=none:proposal-only verdict=none:not-judged commit=none:not-implemented memory=/project/auger/xml-spec-task-tests-gitreins-2026-10-30", "acceptance_criteria": "- **AC-16 (T):** Given a task packet containing in-scope and out-of-scope XML references across multiple files, active and inactive blocks, and unrelated decoys, when Auger assembles the task context, then it returns only the task, in-scope blocks and required graph closure, plus the explicit out-of-scope IDs/reasons; each returned block includes source ID, file, version, and status; proof: `tests/test_task_context.py::test_scope_and_exclusions_are_explicit`.\n- **AC-18 (T):** Given an approved boardctl task and its XML task/test references, when Auger creates the GitReins packet, then the packet preserves the board acceptance criteria verbatim, in/out-of-scope refs, exact test obligations, board ID or explicit ID mapping, and source digests; read-back equals the approved input and repeated export is idempotent; proof: an isolated boardctl/GitReins fixture with byte/digest comparison.\n- **AC-19 (T):** Given a missing, stale, ambiguous, or out-of-scope `ch:trace` reference, when the boardctl→GitReins handoff is requested, then no GitReins judge starts and the result names the invalid row/spec/test IDs; a valid trace starts the existing GitReins lifecycle with the same board acceptance criteria; proof: paired negative/positive integration tests asserting the judge invocation count.\n- **AC-20 (T):** Given a worker summary that claims a test passed while the required migration test is absent or fails on the committed tree, when GitReins evaluates the task packet, then the verdict is not PASS and cites the missing/failed test obligation; proof: a judge-context integration fixture with a deliberately false worker summary and a red migration test.", "depends_on": ["AUG-119", "AUG-120", "AUG-121", "AUG-122", "AUG-123"], "files_changed": [], "foreman_note": "ZERO CODE - GENUINELY UNSTARTED (measured 2026-11-05, HEAD 10ef0d7). 'grep -c boardctl auger.py' -> 0; no task-packet builder, no canonical board-row reader, no digest emitter, no read-back comparator, and AC-16's named proof file tests/test_task_context.py does not exist. The WIRE FORMAT is already defined on the consuming side: GitReins ships engine/auger_packet.py (TaskPacketAdapter) and engine/judge.py::_prepare_auger_task, which fails closed to Tier 1 on PacketValidationError. So the producer must match a real, existing consumer - a worker should read that adapter before designing the packet, and must not invent a second